 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a pause that grows before each retry: 2, 4,
+6 and then 8 seconds (`ATTEMPTS` and `BACKOFF_SECONDS` in `larder/capture.py`). When the fifth attempt times out too,
+the timeout reaches the caller and the pantry order stays uncharged; the
+[gateway timeouts runbook](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md) covers it.
+
+The attempts used to be 3, sent back to back within a second. The gateway answers slowly every Friday from 17:00 to
+19:00, its peak, so all three landed in the same slow minute: one Friday 58 confirmed pantry orders were never
+charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next morning. Switching
+gateways was ruled out while the contract runs, to December 2026. Replaying that Friday's timeouts against the
+gateway's sandbox with 5 attempts spaced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart, 57 of the 58 would have gone through. The cost
+is a member waiting up to 20 seconds longer on the confirmation page, accepted as better than capturing pantry
+orders by hand ([issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md)).
 
